  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Established in 1998, the Business &amp; Hotel Management School (BHMS) is a distinguished private institution in Lucerne, Switzerland. The institution's commitment to academic excellence has been recognised globally, achieving a Five-Star rating in the QS World University Rankings.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>At BHMS, your student life will be engaging, interacting with students from over 80 nationalities. You can also participate in lots of activities and support services to enhance your overall experience. What’s more is that the school organises numerous events throughout the year, such as cooking competitions, themed parties, and excursions to explore Switzerland's landscapes. Plus, the school also offers mental health resources.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>BHMS offers various student accommodations within the historic Union Hotel, now serving as the Lakeside Campus. These include shared standard and superior rooms, and studio apartments. The school also provides off-campus options through its housing partners.</p><p style=\"text-align:center;\"><i>Additionally, if you’re looking for budget-friendly accommodation options outside the campus, feel free to </i><a href=\"https://edvoy.com/app/\"><i>download our app</i></a><i> and check out the Stays feature!</i></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p><strong>Sports</strong><br>At BHMS, you’ll have the opportunity to participate in several sports events. Each year, the school participates in an inter-university sports tournament where you can compete in activities like running, badminton, orienteering, swimming, table tennis, beach volleyball, roundnet (spikeball), uni hockey, and ultimate frisbee. In addition to these, BHMS regularly organises sightseeing and cultural trips.</p><p><strong>Laboratory</strong><br>For those in culinary programs, BHMS offers state-of-the-art facilities, including professional-grade kitchens for every stage of the culinary process.</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong><br>During the week, the City Campus Restaurant offers you three meals a day. On weekends, during term breaks, and holidays, brunch and dinner are served at the Lakeside Campus, giving you a variety of options to enjoy.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
